<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2832" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκᾰθαρ-σία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>uncleanness, foulness</i>,
			of a wound or sore, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				31
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				72c
			</span></i>(pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγγείων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					6.31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>dirt, filth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1117.27
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				13
			</span></i> B.C.), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in
			moral sense, <i>depravity</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.119
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>ceremonial impurity</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Le.</u>
				15.3
			</span></i>,al.</div>
